# RFC 2180 section 4.1.2 says:
#  The server MAY allow the EXPUNGE of a multi-accessed mailbox,
#  and on subsequent FETCH commands return FETCH responses only for
#  non-expunged messages and a tagged NO.
depends 2180base
send 1
a store 1:2 +flags.silent \deleted
receive 1
a OK done
send 1
a uid expunge 1:2
receive 3
* 1 EXPUNGE
* 1 EXPUNGE
a OK done
use watcher
send 1
c fetch 1:3 (uid body.peek[header.fields (date)])
receive 5
* 3 FETCH (UID 3 BODY[HEADER.FIELDS (Date)] {41}
Date: Thu, 27 May 2004 14:28:51 +0200

)
c NO UID(s) 1,2 has/have been expunged
send 1
c fetch 1:3 (uid body.peek[header.fields (date)])
receive 7
* 3 FETCH (UID 3 BODY[HEADER.FIELDS (Date)] {41}
Date: Thu, 27 May 2004 14:28:51 +0200

)
* BYE [CLIENTBUG] These messages have been expunged: 1,2
* OK [CLOSED] I, missa est
c NO UID(s) 1,2 has/have been expunged
end
